							<objPosition posX="53" posY="24"></objPosition>
						</linkSource>
						<linkDestination parentObjectName="TON_FltCnd" pinName="IN">
							<objPosition posX="59" posY="24"></objPosition>
						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<linkFB>
						<linkSource parentObjectName=".2" pinName="OUTP">
							<objPosition posX="53" posY="36"></objPosition>
						</linkSource>
						<linkDestination parentObjectName=".9" pinName="IN1">
							<objPosition posX="59" posY="36"></objPosition>
						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<linkFB>
						<linkSource parentObjectName=".5" pinName="OUT">
							<objPosition posX="55" posY="60"></objPosition>
						</linkSource>
						<linkDestination parentObjectName=".6" pinName="IN1">
							<objPosition posX="59" posY="60"></objPosition>
						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<textBox width="100" height="4">FltCnd is used to generate alarm for HMI / SCADA. 
If iSysFlt is ON, the oHty is turned OFF but the oHMIAlm is not raised (alarm is masked, and there should instead be an associated alarm for the iSysFlt).
The iHMIEnAlm is used for alarm masking requirements.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="51"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="2">Latch the alarm acknowledge output when the alarm output and acknowledge input are on.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="40"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="12" height="4">If the iFlt input pin is not connected, the Heallthy output is turned off.
    <objPosition posX="31" posY="33"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="11">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
   FUNCTION BLOCK - AlmAckIL
***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Description:              Alarm Interlock Function Block
  Change Comments:  Adapted from Yandi Alarm block

***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2019.
***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="3">This DFB monitors a fault signal and turns OFF the Healthy output for interlocking of equipment and Generates Alarm output for HMI/SCADA. The oHty and oHMIAlm are separate signals, which ensures that alarm masking does not impact interlocking of equipment.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="12"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="3">Create fault condition and set healthy output.
Once the iFltDlyTm has expired and FltCnd is raised, the FltCndSL remains ON (while iFlt is ON) even if iSysFlt switches between Off and On. This is important since when iSysFlt is ON, it restarts the timer and turns off FltCnd.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="16"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="15" height="2">Minimum hold-up time for oHMIAlm
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="63"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">Healthy output
    <objPosition posX="66" posY="33"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">HMI Alarm
    <objPosition posX="66" posY="57"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
