					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Network Statistics
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="465"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="15">Map out the Ethernet port and redundancy information for the module

Detect the Rapid Spanning Tree (RSTP) function for each port:
Byte	Bits	Function
1	0/1	ETH1 Port Function
1	2/3	ETH1 RSTP Role
1	4/5	ETH2 Port Function
1	6/7	ETH2 RSTP Role
2	0/1	ETH3 Port Function
2	2/3	ETH3 RSTP Role
2	4/5	ETH Backplane Port Function
2	6/7	ETH Backplane RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="333"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="15" height="19">.

Set the Function code to 3,
Read Holding Registers (4x)




Set the Modbus Address
Location to start reading from



Set the Read Length
12 WORDs
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="59"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="7">The RIO Network Fault (oFlt) is active when:
- The Network is Enabled; AND
- Either:
   - Both Ethernet Links are Disconnected; OR
   - The RIO Scanner is Unhealthy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="498"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH2 Port Function
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="352"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">Out Count
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="470"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="28">Map out the useful health of the services running on the CPU module. These statuses are only mapped out for Engineer diagnostics and are not meant to be displayed on the HMI.

WORD	Bit	Description
1	0	RSTP Service Healthy or Disabled
1	1	Spare
1	2	Port 502 Service Healthy or Disabled
1	3	SNMP Service Healthy or Disabled
1	4	Main IP Address Healthy (Not Unassigned or Duplicate)
1	5	Spare
1	6	Spare
1	7	Ethernet IP Scanner Healthy or Disabled
1	8	Modbus Scanner Healthy or Disabled
1	9	Spare
1	10	SNTP Service Healthy or Disabled
1	11	Web Server Healthy or Disabled
1	12	Firmware Upgrade Service Healthy or Disabled
1	13	FTP Service Healthy or Disabled
1	14	FDR Service Healthy or Disabled
1	15	Ethernet IP Adapter Service Healthy
2	0	Redundant IO IP Address Healthy (Not Unassigned or Duplicate)
2	1	LLDP Service Healthy or Disabled
2	2	Event Log Service Healthy or Disabled
2	3	Log Service (SysLog) Not Reachable
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="403"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="9">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.11	BCY	14/01/2026	Changed iStsDDT Type from T_BMENOC0301_3 to T_BMENOC0301_4
1.10	AXY	17/10/2022	Updated status link OK logic for service port use; in accordance to RTIO standard
1.00	NJA	01/04/2020	Initial Release<objPosition posX="0" posY="41"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="5">Generate the ADDM_TYPE Address Array for the transaction
This is done manually as using string functions to generate an input string for the ADDM EFB is very difficult.
The ADDM string we are replicating is: '0.[PLMID].0{127.0.0.1}100.TCP.MBS'
This uses the loopback address to query the NOC via Modbus at slave ID 100.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="100"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="6">The RIO Network is Healthy (oOK) Provided:
- The Network is Enabled; AND
- Either of the Ethernet Links are Connected; AND
- The RIO Scanner  is Healthy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="481"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH3 Port Function
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="380"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="21" height="5">Link Status for Communications fault generation depending on Ethernet Mode:
	0: Default, service port (Ethernet 1)
	1: Network Device Ports (Ethernet 2, 3)
    <objPosition posX="9" posY="325"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Determine the health of the data
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="233"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Determine the status of the comms exchange.
This is done at the start of the DFB as it allows the PLC one scan to complete the request.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="158"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="15" height="27">.

Determine if the exchange is active




Check for communication errors.




Detect if a successful exchange has occurred




Detect if an unsuccessful exchange has occurred
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="162"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">Map the IP Address read from the drive
The IP address is located at WORDs 40006 - 40007
Only update the values on a successful exchange and clear the values when the data becomes invalid.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="248"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Control the comms exchange
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="191"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH3 RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="379"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="24" height="14">Port Function (ETHxFunc) Codes:
0:  Disabled
1:  Access Port
2:  Port Mirror
3:  RIO Network (Used as part of RSTP loop)

RSTP Role (LnkxSts) Codes:
0:  Alternate
1:  Backup
2:  Designated (Outward port away from CPU)
3:  Root (Inward port towards CPU)
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="387"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">Out Error Count
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="475"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH2 RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="358"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">An explicit data comms request is used to determine the IP address of the NOC module.

Set the Modbus parameters for the Explicit transaction.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="54"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">Map out the Ethernet port information for the module

Detect which ports are connected:
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="285"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="15" height="19">.
Pack the Modbus parameters into Send Data for the DATA_EXCH instruction.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="79"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="26">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================
The BME NOC0301 is used to communicate with devices on an Ethernet Network. The BMENOC0301 DFB object retrieves status information from the NOC. The diagnostic data is read from the NOC0301 Device DDT called T_BMENOC0301_4 and via an explicit Modbus read to the NOC diagnostic registers.

The DFB monitors the status of the Ethernet links, the NOC IO Scanner and communications to the module to determine the Healthy (oOK) status and the Faulted (oFlt) status of the NOC0301 module. The NOC Enable (iEn) pin is used to delay the Healthy (oOK) and Fault (oFlt) statuses of the NOC until the PLC has finished initialising on startup.

The Module Slot Number (iPLMID) is required for the explicit Modbus read to the NOC module. Note: This DFB will only work if the NOC is located in the head rack of the PLC. The explicit read reads the IP address of the module. The IP address is available via the IP Address (oIPAdr) pin.

The Ethernet Link Active statuses (oLnkxAct) show the link active statuses of Ethernet ports ETH2 and ETH3.<objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
