					<textBox width="90" height="4">System Overhead Scan Time
Get the system overhead scan time from the CPU status registers to calculate the average scan time over a period of 100 PLC scans, and also the maximum and minimum values over the runtime of the PLC. Setting the reset variable to 1 resets the maximum and minimum scan time values.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="349"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="13">Convert the Pulse Time intervals from TIME to DINT values.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="419"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="31">%S18  Overflow or Arithmetic Error: Normally set to 0, this bit is set to 1 in the event of a capacity overflow of any data type or a divide by zero.  The user must reset this bit to 0.


%S20  Index Overflow: Normally set to 0, this bit is set to 1 when the address of the indexed object becomes less than 0 or exceeds the number of objects declared in the configuration. The user must reset this bit to 0.


%S39  Saturation in Event Processing: This bit is set to 1 by the system to indicate that one or more events cannot be processed following saturation of the queues.  The PLC logic must reset this bit to 0.


%S78  Stop In The Event Of Error: This bit is used to instruct the CPU to halt on %15 (Character String Fault), %S18 (Overflow or Arithmetic Error) and %20 (Index Overflow) errors. This is set to zero to prevent halting the CPU.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="119"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="24">As Freerun is a microsecond value, divide by 1000 to work in milliseconds.
If the value is negative (ie Freerun has wrapped), then add double the wrap value to calculate the scan value.









If the value is outside the range of 1 and 5000 then ignore the value as the FreeRunOld value has been reset or the PLC has been in STOP mode (ie value is 0 - no change or greater than 5 seconds)
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="272"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Pulse Generation
Use the Scan Time value calculated in the section above to accumulate times for each pulse interval value. The Done pulse is set when the accumulated time is greater than or equal to the preset pulse interval value. When Done, the accumulated value greater then the preset value is rolled over to ensure accuracy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="414"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="46">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================
The BMEP586x4x DFB object retrieves status information from a Modicon BMX P586x4x M580 processor and configures basic settings in the processor.

The PLC DFB generates the following statuses:
•  Set a first scan status (oFstScn);
•  Set a PLC initialisation complete status (oSttOK);
•  Resettable current, minimum, maximum and average scan times for the PLC cyclic task (oScnXxx);
•  Resettable current, minimum, maximum and average scan times for the PLC overheads (oSysScnXxx);
•  Generate a PLC Arithmetic or Overflow Fault (oSys1Flt);
•  Generate a PLC Index Overflow Fault (oSys2Flt);
•  Generate an SD Card Fault status (oMemFlt);
•  Generate four accurate system pulses (iPlsxVal/oPlsx);
•  Generate a PLC Watchdog value (oPLCWD);
•  Display time and date of last PLC modification (oCfgTm);
•  Display configuration ID of last PLC modification (oCfgID); and
•  IP Address of the Main Network Interface (oIPAdr).

And, the PLC DFB manages the following settings:
•  Resets PLC Arithmetic or Overflow Faults;
•  Resets PLC Index Overflow Faults;
•  Resets Saturation in Event Processing Faults;
•  Configures the PLC not to Stop in the Event of Error; and
•  Instructs the PLC to back up the program to the SD card.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Write out to the Status &amp; Control WORD.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="504"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Break out the Control word into the applicable commands.  Note that the commands are reset after use within the ScanTimes section.  Also pulse the reset on first scan to initialise the scan time statistics.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="88"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="13">==========================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK -	BMEP586x4x
==========================================================================================================================================
Description:		BME P586x4x M580 Processor Status &amp; Diagnostics
Date Changed:		14/01/2026
Change Comments:	Changed iStsDDT Type to match BME P58 6040 v4.40 Device DDT
Revision:			1.01

==========================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2026
==========================================================================================================================================<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="7">%SW27  System Overhead Time: The last system overhead time.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="354"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="7">Set the minimum value since last reset, or set to the current scan value upon resetting via the HMI.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="307"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="21">.








Reset the Scan Reset command to 0 to ensure it is only active for one scan.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="508"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="4">Scan Time Information
Using the FREERUN function to ensure accuracy of values, calculate the average scan time over a period of 100 PLC scans, and also the maximum and minimum values over the runtime of the PLC. Setting the reset variable to 1 resets the maximum and minimum scan time values.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="267"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="22">%SW6  	IP3, IP4









%SW7  	IP1, IP2
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="228"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="30">Calculate the average scan time by looking at 100 scans worth.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="316"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="9">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.01	BCY	14/01/2026	Changed iStsDDT Type to match BME P58 6040 v4.40 Device DDT
1.00	NJA	01/04/2020	Initial Release<objPosition posX="0" posY="61"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">The use of the standard PRJ_VERS FB shall be used to indicate the date and time of the last download of the PLC program, either online changes or full download.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="197"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">The IP address of the Main Ethernet port on the CPU in byte format
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="224"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="7">Set the maximum system overhead scan value since last reset, or set to zero upon resetting via the HMI.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="363"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">The bit %S21 indicates the first cycle of this task, including after a cold start with automatic start in run and a warm start. %S21 is set to 1 at the start of the first PLC cycle and reset to zero at the end of that cycle.  Generate a state that indicates the PLC has completed initialisation after a restart that can be used to ensure communications has been restored before attempting to start the plant or generate fault statuses.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="74"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="7">Set the minimum system overhead scan value since last reset, or set to the current scan value upon resetting via the HMI.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="372"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Diagnostic information is provided by system bits (%S) and words (%SW) within the CPU.  Some of the more important alarm status bits are exposed as variables to allow for alarming on the HMI.  Statuses requiring resetting by the user manually are also reset here.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="115"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Generate the heart beat value for this PLC. It can be used for:
- Inter PLC communications
- in the HMI to determine PLC running status.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="253"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="7">Set the maximum scan value since last reset, or set to zero upon resetting via the HMI.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="298"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="30">Calculate the average system overhead scan time by looking at 100 scans worth.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="381"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="67">Use the Scan Time value calculated in the section above to accumulate times for each pulse interval value. The Done pulse is set when the accumulated time is greater than or equal to the preset pulse interval value.  When Done, the accumulated value greater then the preset value is rolled over to ensure accuracy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="434"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Ensure the project backup on the SD Card is consistent with the CPU project.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="153"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="37">%S96  Backup Project OK: the card is correct and the application is consistent with CPU Internal Application RAM.




Check if there is an SD Card error
%SW97  Card Status: Indicates the status of the card. 0000=No Error




If the projects are not consistent, initiate a SD card backup.
%S66  Application Backup: Start a SD Card backup operation. This bit is set to 0 by the system when the backup is finished.
Note: The EN pin of the MOVE instruction is used because %S66 must not be written to when %S66 is TRUE. The logic must test that bit %S66 has been set to 0 by the system before doing a write.


If the SD Card does not become healthy after a delay, generate an error.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="157"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
