					<textBox width="70" height="6">The RIO Network Redundancy Error is active (oRdnErr) provided
- The Network is Enabled.
- The Network Redundancy is NOT Healthy (masked by Service port Mode).
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="290"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="4">Map out the Ethernet port, redundancy and service information for the module

Detect which ports are connected, and generate an Ethernet Link Configuration Error if the ethernet link is active to a different port defined by iEthMode
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="54"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="9">The RIO Network Fault (oFlt) is active when
- The Network is Enabled, and either
   - Ethernet Configuration Error
   - There is no Ethernet Link Active
   - Ethernet Backplane Failure
   - IP Address status (Duplicate or No IP configured)
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="318"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">Out Error Count
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="256"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH2 RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="162"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="71" height="23">Write out to the Status WORD.

Bit	Description
0	IO Scanner Service Healthy
1	Redundancy Healthy
2	Remote IO IP Address Healthy
3	Network Broadcast Storm Not Detected
4	FDR Service Healthy or Disabled (Service pushes configurations to CRA modules on power up)
5	ETH1 Port Active (Service Port)
6	ETH2 Port Active
7	ETH3 Port Active
8	
9	
10	
11	
12	
13	
14	
15
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="374"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">In Count
    <objPosition posX="26" posY="250"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH3 RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="177"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="26">Description:
**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
The BME P586x4x M580 processor supports Remote IO networks through the front Ethernet ports. The BMEP586x4xRIO DFB object retrieves status information from the processor about the state of the RIO network. The diagnostic data is read from the processor Device DDT called T_BMEP58_ECPU_EXT2.

The DFB monitors the status of the Ethernet links and the IO Scanner to determine the Healthy (oOK) status and the Faulted (oFlt) status of the RIO network. The Network Enable (iEn) pin is used to delay the Healthy (oOK) and Fault (oFlt) statuses of the network until the PLC has finished initialising on startup.

Set ethernet connection mode (iEthMode = 0) for connection via service port, or (iEthMode = 1) for connection via network device port (ethernert port 2, 3). Fault status (oFlt) is set active when the ethernet module status and ethernet mode configuration is not consistent. E.g., iEthMode = 0 (service port mode) and oLnk2Act = 1 --&gt; oFlt = 1.

The Ethernet Link Active statuses (oLnkxAct) show the link active statuses of Ethernet ports ETH1, ETH2 and ETH3. The Maintenance Fault (oMntFlt) status reports if there are issues with the network but may not directly impact the service, including loss of redundancy, an IP address conflict, a network broadcast storm, or an FDR Service fault.<objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="24" height="14">Port Function (ETHxFunc) Codes:
0:  Disabled
1:  Access Port
2:  Port Mirror
3:  RIO Network (Used as part of RSTP loop)

RSTP Role (LnkxSts) Codes:
0:  Alternate
1:  Backup
2:  Designated (Outward port away from CPU)
3:  Root (Inward port towards CPU)
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="175"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="11">**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
   FUNCTION BLOCK - BMEP586x4xRIO
**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Description:         BME P586x4x M580 Processor RIO Remote IO Network Status
  Reviison:         	1.11
 
**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2026.
**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">Out Count
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="250"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="7">The RIO block is healthy (oOK) provided
- The Network is Enabled.
- No faults active.
- The RIO IP address is healthy.
-  A Network Broadcast Storm is NOT detected.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="350"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="21" height="6">Ethernet Link Configuration Error depending on Ethernet Mode:
- 0: Default, service port (Ethernet 1)
- 1: Network Device Ports (Ethernet 2, 3)
    <objPosition posX="68" posY="100"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="28">Map out the useful health of the services running on the CPU module. These statuses are only mapped out for Engineer diagnostics and are not meant to be displayed on the HMI.

WORD	Bit	Description
1	0	RSTP Service Healthy or Disabled
1	1	Spare
1	2	Port 502 Service Healthy or Disabled
1	3	SNMP Service Healthy or Disabled
1	4	Main IP Address Healthy (Not Unassigned or Duplicate)
1	5	Ethernet Backplane Hardware Healthy
1	6	Ethernet Backplane Healthy
1	7	Ethernet IP Scanner Healthy
1	8	Modbus Scanner Healthy
1	9	NTP Service Healthy
1	10	SNTP Service Healthy
1	11	Web Server Healthy
1	12	Firmware Upgrade Service Healthy
1	13	FTP Service Healthy
1	14	FDR Service Healthy
1	15	Ethernet IP Adapter Service Healthy
2	0	Remote IO IP Address Healthy (Not Unassigned or Duplicate)
2	1	LLDP Service Healthy or Disabled
2	2	Event Log Service Healthy or Disabled
2	3	Log Service (SysLog) Not Reachable
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="190"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="6">The RIO Scanner is Healthy (oScnOK) provided
- The Network is Enabled.
- The IO Scanner  is Healthy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="272"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH1 Port Function
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="140"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH3 Port Function
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="170"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="9">Revision History
**************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
1.11	BCY	14/01/2026		Changed iStsDDT Type to match BME P58 6040 v4.40 Device DDT
1.10	AXY	04/05/2023		Included input option to select between use of service port or network ports
1.00	NJA	01/04/2020		Initial Release<objPosition posX="0" posY="41"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH2 Port Function
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="155"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="3">Network Statistics
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="245"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">In Error Count
    <objPosition posX="26" posY="256"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="9" height="2">ETH1 RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="61" posY="147"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="15">Map out the Ethernet port and redundancy information for the module

Detect the Rapid Spanning Tree (RSTP) function for each port:
Byte	Bits	Function
1	0/1	ETH1 Port Function
1	2/3	ETH1 RSTP Role
1	4/5	ETH2 Port Function
1	6/7	ETH2 RSTP Role
2	0/1	ETH3 Port Function
2	2/3	ETH3 RSTP Role
2	4/5	ETH Backplane Port Function
2	6/7	ETH Backplane RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="123"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
