					<textBox width="80" height="5">Map out the general CRA State:
CRA_STATE:  Running state of the CRA module
Note: This generally follows the running state of the CPU.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="113"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Map out the CRA module firmware.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="365"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="23">Write out to the Status WORD.

Bit	Description
0	Module ID Switch Changed During Run
1	
2	
3	
4	
5	ETH1 Port Active - (03/05/2023) AXY
6	ETH2 Port Active
7	ETH3 Port Active
8	
9	
10	
11	
12	
13	
14	
15
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="425"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="15">Map out the Ethernet port and redundancy information for the module

Detect the Rapid Spanning Tree (RSTP) function for each port:
Bits	Function
0/1	ETH1 Port Function
2/3	ETH1 RSTP Role
4/5	ETH2 Port Function
6/7	ETH2 RSTP Role
8/9	ETH3 Port Function
10/11	ETH3 RSTP Role
12/13	ETH Backplane Port Function
14/15	ETH Backplane RSTP Role
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="263"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="9">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.00	NJA	01/04/2020	Initial Release
1.10	AXY	03/05/2023	Edited block, included input option to select between use of service port or network ports; 
				Changed output status DDT to display ETH1 status (oSts.Lnk1Sts)
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="51"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="6">Map out the general CRA Diagnositcs:
CRA_DIAGNOSTIC:  CRA Diagnostic WORD
4:  Rotary Switch Position Changed
5:  Modules Comms Healthy (AKA DROP_COM_HEALTH)
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="152"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">Map out the Ethernet port and redundancy information for the module

Detect which ports are connected:
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="204"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Map out the health of the services running on the CRA module. These statuses are only mapped out for Engineer diagnostics and are not meant to be displayed on the HMI.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="325"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="21" height="8">Ethernet Link Configuration Error
depending on Ethernet Mode:
	0: Default, service port (Ethernet 1)
	1: Network Device Ports (Ethernet 2, 3)
Masked if no Ethernet Link Active (Comms fault); AND Data read back is valid.
    <objPosition posX="68" posY="245"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="8">The module fault (oFlt) is active when:
- Communications to the unit is healthy
     - Module is NOT Running, OR
     - The Rotary Position Switch has changed
OR
     - Ethernet Link is not consistent with iEthMode Configuration
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="400"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Detect the drop Index. The drop index is determined by the position of the rotary switches on startup.
Latch in the Rotary Switch position while the switch position is not different from the startup position.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="185"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="7">The module status is healthy (oOK) provided:
- Communications to the unit is healthy
- Module is Running
- The Rotary Position Switch has NOT changed
- Ethernet Link is not consistent with iEthMode Configuration
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="381"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="36">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================
The BMXCRA31210 DFB object provides diagnostic and monitoring data for a BMX CRA31210 Redundant IO Network Ethernet Module. This includes monitoring of Ethernet ports, module status and network breaks.

Set ethernet connection mode (iEthMode = 0) for connection via service port, or (iEthMode = 1) for connection via network device port (ethernert port 2, 3). Fault status (oFlt) is set active when the ethernet module status and ethernet mode configuration is not consistent. E.g., iEthMode = 0 (service port mode) and oLnk2Act = 1 --&gt; oFlt = 1.

When communications to the module are healthy, the Data Valid Status (oDatOK) is set active. When communications to the module are unhealthy, the Communications Fault status (oComFlt) is set active. Both statuses are inactive when the RIO Network is unhealthy (NOT iNetOK). (Note Communications Fault will only trigger if there is more than one RIO drop active and helathy in the PLC).

When the module is healthy, the Healthy Status (oLnkOK) is set active. When the module has a fault, the Fault status (oFlt) is set active. Both statuses are inactive communications are unhealthy (NOT oDatOK).

A Powering Up status (oPwrUp) is generated when the power supply to the module has reactivated (iPwrOK). During the Power Up duration, the Communications Fault status (oComFlt) is masked.

The CRA module drop number (oIdx/oSts.Idx) is displayed.

The two Ethernet port connections are monitored and the Link Active statuses (oLnkxAct) are active when there is a connection present on the ports.

The Status DDT (oSts) contains additional CRA status information, including:
	1.  Module Firmware version (oSts.Cfg) in the format (x.xx):
	2.  port Rapid Spaning Tree Roles (oSts.LnkxSts);
	3.  Module State (oSts.ModSts); and
		a.  1 = Idle
		b.  2 = Stopped
		c.  3 = Running
	4.  Module ID Switch Changed During Run (oSts.IdxErr).
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">RPI for packets from IO Scanner to CRA module.
Note: The RPI for packets from CRA module to IO scanner is found on the 'Parameters' tab of the CRA configuration window.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="345"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="13">==========================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK -	BMXCRA31210
==========================================================================================================================================
Description:		BMX CRA31210 RIO Redundant IO Drop Ethernet Module Status
Date Changed:		03/05/2023
Change Comments:	Initial Release
Revision:		1.10

==========================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2020
==========================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="6">The communications fault (oFlt) is active when:
- the connection that is used to read the words from the unit is unhealthy; and
- both the status of the communications module (iPLMOK) and the power supply for the unit (iPwrOK) are healthy for 15s.
The delay is required to prevent the communication fault activating during the unit's self test cycle, and indicated by the start up status (oPwrUp).
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="82"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="24" height="14">Port Function (ETHxFunc) Codes:
0:  Disabled
1:  Access Port
2:  Port Mirror
3:  RIO Network (Used as part of RSTP loop)

RSTP Role (LnkxSts) Codes:
0:  Alternate
1:  Backup
2:  Designated (Outward port away from CPU)
3:  Root (Inward port towards CPU)
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="287"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="7">Communications to the unit are healthy when:
- the status of the communications module used (iPLMOK) is healthy
- the connection that is used to read the words from the unit (LnkOK) is healthy.

When communications is unhealthy, all values read from the unit are invalid and set to zero.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="61"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
