					<textBox width="110" height="5">The BACS and Cordex Interface Communications fault (oComFlt) is active when:
- the connection that is used to read the data from the interface is unhealthy; 
- both the status of the communications module (iPLMOK) and the power supply for the unit (iPwrOK) are healthy for 15s.
The delay is required to prevent the communication fault activating while the unit's starting up.<objPosition posX="0" posY="102"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="7">Cordex GEST1 &amp; 2 [2] flickers between 2 and 0 for up to 20s on comms loss before settling on 7.

Use RS latch prevent CordexComFlt from flickering.<objPosition posX="80" posY="144"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="36">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
The EPT CCS110 4.4 kW N+1 Mine Spec Unit is an IP42‑rated charger system featuring a single‑phase AC input and a regulated 110 VDC output, designed for high‑reliability mining and industrial applications. It is monitored through 2 interfaces, the Cordex CXC-HP System Controller and the Generex CS141 BACS WEBMANAGER unit via Modbus TCP. This DFB reads the Cordex and BACS data and presents it in the required format for use by the rest of the PLC program and/or by the HMI.

This DFB is specific to the Brockman Syncline 1 (BS1) project implementation of 1 string of 9 BACS modules, as per the following drawings:
BR4-2110-E-00742 PRIMARY CRUSHING SUBSTATION BSR130 BSR130BC02 BATTERY CHARGER CIRCUIT DIAGRAM
BR4-1860-E-00428 NPI HUB SWITCHROOM BSR131 BSR131BC01 BATTERY CHARGER CIRCUIT DIAGRAM
BR4-2150-E-01604 OVERLAND CONVEYOR SUBSTATION BSR132 BSR132BC01 BATTERY CHARGER CIRCUIT DIAGRAM

---

Cordex CXC-HP System Controller data mapping is based on the following document:
Name:		Cordex® HP Controller Modbus Integrator Guide
ID:		0350114-J0
Version:		01/2025
FIlename:	en-m-amer-cordexhpcontrollermodbus-0350114-j0

The following data will be read:
Alarms (Discrete Inputs Addresses 15000 - 15187)
Analogues (Input Register Addresses 35000 - 35075)

---

Generex CS141 data mapping is based on the following document:
Name:		GENEREX Comprehensive User Manuals
Version:		v.2025-09-18 FW2.16-2.26
FIlename:	manual_CS141_en incl modbus

The following data will be read:
BACS System - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1000 - 1005)
BACS String 1 - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1010 - 1013)
BACS Modules 1 - 9 - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1060 - 1104)<objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="9">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	09/07/2026	Initial Release<objPosition posX="0" posY="51"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Map Cordex status and alarm registers for decoding and generate Cordex statuses from it

Cordex healthy when:
- Data read back from the Cordex CXC-HP System Controller is healthy;
- Cordex alarm registers are reporting 0.<objPosition posX="9" posY="170"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="4">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
BACS Status Mapping
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="205"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="7">Communications to the CCS110 unit's BACS and Cordex interfaces are healthy when:
- the status of the communications module used is healthy
- the connection that is used to read data from the interface is healthy

When an interface's communications is unhealthy, all values read from that interface are invalid and set to zero.<objPosition posX="0" posY="61"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="4">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
Cordex Status Mapping
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="165"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="13">==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK - CCS110
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Description:	      CCS110 Battery Charger
Date Changed:	      09/07/2026	
Change Comments:      Initial Release
Revision:	      1.00

==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2026
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Map BACS status and alarm registers for decoding and generate BACS statuses from it

BACS healthy when:
- Data read back from the CS141 BACS Webmanager unit is healthy;
- BACS system is running; and
- BACS alarm registers are reporting 0.<objPosition posX="10" posY="210"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
