					<textBox width="100" height="11">Combined Command Word and Initilisation on First Scan
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
Combine with all bits (or specific bits) of Group command word
To combine with all bits of group command word, set iGrpCmdEn to 16#FFFF.
An example of combining with specific bits of Group command word is to prevent group commands from changing mode of auxiliary equipment to Local. (Set iGrpCmdEn with hex code that enables all bits except local mode selection)

Upon First scan (%S21), initialise oCmdWd to iInitCmd.
Typically, equipment are initialised to either Local or Auto
