					<textBox width="26" height="14">Sequence Status Word Mapping
==========================
The sequence status are coded with two bits for HMI display.

State                                      Seq2          Seq1 
=====================================
Error (Unused)                            0                 0    
Sequence Enabled                    0                 1    
Sequence Stopping                   1                 0    
Sequence Disabled                    1                 1
    <objPosition posX="24" posY="75"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="17">Drive Status Word Mapping
=====================
The status are coded with three bits for HMI display.

State                                      Stat3          Stat2         Stat1
=============================================
Out of Service                           0                 0               0
Auto Ready                               0                 0               1                           Auto Running                            0                 1               0
Starting                                     0                 1               1
Unacknowledged Faulted          1                 0               0
Acknowledged Faulted              1                 0               1
Maintenance Ready                  1                 1               0
Maintenance Running               1                 1               1
    <objPosition posX="45" posY="33"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="34" height="7">Drive Status
=======================
This section includes the logic for  building of mode, status and sequence words for HMI display (using a single word)
New version for AMES DrvFwd_BF DFB.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="8" height="3">Map Aut and Man to Aut Status
    <objPosition posX="20" posY="17"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="26" height="5">Drive Status Word
==============
All Drive Status bits are packed into a single word. Each bit can be assigned a variable tag in the HMI.
    <objPosition posX="24" posY="96"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="18" height="3">Unpack bits from drive status output words
=================================
    <objPosition posX="85" posY="10"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
