					<textBox width="100" height="4">Warning Siren Output.
==================
The warning siren must be active for a certain time before the drive will start.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="310"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="8">Manual Run Seal.
============
The manual run seal starts the drive in MANUAL mode.
The start sequence interlock must be satisfied before the drive will start, but once started the drive will continue to run without it.
The run sequence interlock are required before the drive will run.
The drive will stop as soon as the run sequence interlock is off.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="245"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="13" height="2">Fault While Drive is Stopped
    <objPosition posX="81" posY="157"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="5">Drive Run Off
===========
The drive run off is used to ensure that during a sequence shutdown, the ore is run off the equipment before shutting down.  The timer is started once the upstream equipment is deemed run off and times the period for this drive to have run off the ore before indicating that it is run off.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="383"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="15">*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
   FUNCTION BLOCK - DrvFwd_BF
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Description:                Drive Forward for Brownfields
  Change Comments:    Adapted from DrvFwd Standard DFB, aligned to brownfields control requirements

*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2019.
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************

Rev 1.02 - DrvMov status created to prevent drive restart until stationary
Rev 1.01 - Local Stop Pushbutton input and Auto Ready status added
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Fault Seal &amp; Reset Required
=======================
The fault seal self latches whenever the drive faults in Auto mode or a critical interlock faults in Local mode OR if the drive losses its auxiliary drive ready while it is running.
In Auto or Manual mode once the fault has been cleared the Reset Required status will become healthy indicating to the controller that a fault acknowledge from the HMI is available to unlatch the Fault Seal.
In Local mode the fault will reset automatically when the fault has been cleared.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="137"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="27" height="3">On transition to Auto mode only active Group Start Seal if the drive is running and Sequence Run Interlock is healthy.
    <objPosition posX="4" posY="209"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="8" height="3">Detect First Scan
=============
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="29"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Reset Required
    <objPosition posX="81" posY="146"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="5">Group Start Seal.
=============
The group start seal latches up when the drive has been started as part of the group in AUTO mode.
The shutdown sequence interlocks are placed in the run off logic so as to hold the drive running until the required order in a sequenced shutdown.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="197"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="5">Group Stop Seal.
==============
The Group Stop Seal is active in Auto only, and is set by the HMI to initiate the sequenced shutdown of the plant. 
Once the group stop seal is latched the drive will continue to start and stop based on the sequence start and run interlocks, waiting until the sequence stop interlock is true before unlatching the group start seal.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="119"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="4">Drive &amp; HMI Commands.
======================
The commands from the HMI are mapped into a command word which is unpacked to the individual commands here.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="36"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="8">Auto Run Seal.
============
The auto run seal starts the drive in AUTO mode as part of a group start.
The start sequence interlock must be satisfied before the drive will start, but once started the drive will continue to run without it.
The run sequence interlock are required before the drive will run.
The drive will stop as soon as the run sequence interlock is off.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="226"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Local Forward Run Seal.
=================================
When in LOCAL mode the drive is started from the field start pushbutton, provided the local start and run interlocks and the drive critical interlocks are all healthy.
To allow the control room operator to shutdown the drive remotely if necessary the drive stop and group crash stop controls unlatch the start seal.
If the Local Run Interlock goes off the local run seal is unlatched.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="272"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="5">Fault Reset Output
=================
In Auto or Manual mode the operator will acknowledge the fault from the HMI; In Local and Out of Service mode the fault will automatically reset.
The oFltRst output shall be used to reset all alarms associated with the drive.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="181"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="12">Standard Drive Logic Control
=======================
This section includes the logic for starting and stopping the drive. External logic passes the critical and non-critical interlocks which have the following characteristics:
- The critical interlocks fault the drive in any mode.
- The non-critical interlocks only fault the drive in AUTO and MANUAL mode.
Also the Sequence interlocks are passed in, comprising of:
- The Sequence Start Interlock: is required as well as the Sequence Run IL before the drive will start and is ignored once the drive is running.
- The Sequence Run Interlock: is required for the drive to run.
- The Sequence Stop Interlock: in conjunction with the Group Stop Seal allows the drive to shutdown in sequence order.
- Manual and local modes have their respective start and run interlocks.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="16"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="6">Auxiliary Drive Fault While Running
============================
The previous implementation of the auxiliary drive could provide a situation with the drive running and a momentary loss of the iAuxDrvRdy would result in the drive cycling ON and OFF without tripping the drive. This logic will produce a one scan pulse that will trip the drive internally and provide an external output for the user to program into an alarm for connection to the drive interlocks.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="330"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="5">Fault Acknowledged
=================
In Auto or Manual mode the controller will issue a fault acknowledge from the HMI to latch a fault acknowledged status if the drive is still faulted.
Additionally in Auto or Manual mode if a fault occurs while the drive is stopped than an Fault While Stopped status will be latched in order to automatically reset the drive when it becomes healthy again.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="165"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="9">Auxiliary Drive Start Output.
======================
The auxiliary drive start output is held active once the siren time is complete.

Run Output.
======================
The run output is only activated once the siren time is complete, and the auxiliary drive ready input is active is complete.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="345"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Fault Latch
    <objPosition posX="41" posY="146"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="26" height="6">Auto Sequence Siren Pre-Start
=========================
Start-up times can be minimised by bringing in a iSeqPreStt to turn the siren on at:
      Previous Drive RunUp Time - Current Drive Siren Time.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="323"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="10">Drive Mode States.
===============
The drive can be in one of the four modes: AUTO, MANUAL, LOCAL and OOS. The drive can be switched between AUTO, MANUAL and LOCAL modes on the run. OOS mode can not be selected when the drive is running.

HMI AUTO, MANUAL and LOCAL mode commands.
==========================================
These modes can be selected from either the individual drive mode control or the group controls.
When the drive is OOS the group control selection is disabled.  This has the effect of removing the drive from the group.  To place the drive back in either AUTO, MANUAL or LOCAL, the individual drive mode control must be used.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="63"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="3">Local Run Seal &amp; Forward Run Seal Status
===================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="297"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="3">Auto, Manual &amp; Local  Running Output
===============================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="405"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="4">Drive Run Up Output.
=================
Once the main contactor has closed the drive is allowed a period of time to run up to speed. The drive run up coil is typically used in the run sequence interlocks of the next upstream drive. If Run up time is overridden, drive is considered run up
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="363"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
