					<textBox width="50" height="11">Ensure that the operator adjustable output value is kept in sync with the PID output when in auto mode to ensure bumpless transfer.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="285"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="45" height="68">.
Differential Contribution


0 = Bumpless Transition to Auto Mode
1 = Transition to Auto Mode with Bump



Dead Zone on Deviation



Reduction in KP within Dead Zone


Reduce the Overrun



Manual Compensation



Lower Limit of the Output



Upper Limit of the Output


Limit for Output Modification in
Units per Sec (&gt;=0)


Lower Limit of Feed Forward Range


Upper Limit of Feed Forward Range


Lower Limit of Feed Forward Output
Range


Upper Limit of Feed Forward Output
Range
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="96"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="10">Ensure that if Feed Forward component is non zero that it is capped to the limit set.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="240"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="11">When in Cascade mode, the cascade setpoint is used for control, and is written to the main setpoint such that switching back to auto mode results in a seemless change over.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="210"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="24">Break out the command word into the applicable commands.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="41"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="17">If in Manual mode, the output value entered by the operator is limited to a rate of change value (iROC).  When in auto, pass the value straight through the block to ensure bumpless transfer when sswitching to Manual mode.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="222"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="45" height="68">.
Reserved for Autotuning


Lower Limit of the Process Value Range



Upper Limit of the Process Value Range



Lower Limit of the Output Value Range



Upper Limit of the Output Value Range


0 = Direct Acting Controller
1 = Reverse Acting Controller


0 = Mixed Structure Controller
1 = Parallel Structure Controller



Anti-windup Halt is Filtered - set to one


RCPY input is not used - set to zero


Proportional Action Coefficient (Gain)



Integral Time



Derivative Time



Differential Gain
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="96"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="40">K_PID  {v(G) = 5}
*********************

The PID object carries out the requirements for the Proportional, Integral, Derivative (PID) control algorithm with series structure.  The object shall;
- Allow for direct and reverse action of the PID controller
- Allow for Auto, Manual and Cascade modes of operation
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="44">The PID Controller is only enabled when the start condition is true, and prior to the start being completed, the output is set to that of the start up value.  The PID Controller is auto enabled provided startup is complete, the process related conditions are true (iEnAut) and the loop is not in Manual (Cascade operation requires the loop to be in auto mode internally).  The start up delay can be overridden if required, such as if the PV &gt; SP while starting.  
Set the start delay to a minimum of 1 second.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="165"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="23">Clear the control commands, and map the PID status information into the control word.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="297"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="33">The output value of the PID controller is set as follows:
- PID output passed through K, I, D when in auto, startup complete and auto enabled.
- Start Up reference when starting and in auto mode.
- Operator reference when in manual mode or startup complete and not auto enabled.
- Minimum output value when not required.

The switch between auto and manual modes is carried out by the tracking input and hence the input MAN_AUTO is always true.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="251"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="10">24/11/20 - 0813 - MBT - Enabled FF control option
14/08/13 - 1838 - MCG - Changed anti-windup type, and gain structure
22/07/13 - 14:00 - MBT - Corrected Restart functionality
05/04/13 10:57 - BSN - Revision changed to meet STD-J-010.  Added iReStt pin to restart the iStt command when PID lop is already running.   
Rev A.3  MBT 06/09/11 - Corrected Cascade Operation on startup
Rev A.2  MBT 09/08/11 - Added ability to override startup delay
Rev A.1  MBT 02/06/11 - Merged Commands and Status
Rev A.0  MBT 21/03/11 - Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="91" height="2">Parameterise the PID block, mapping the data into the pre-defined Para_PIDFF DDT.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="93"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="50" height="26">Determine the mode of operation for the PID controller, with the default mode being Auto.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="66"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
