					<textBox width="110" height="62">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
The MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker EIFE (Embedded Ethernet Interface for Drawout Devices) is a communication module that connects MasterPact MTZ drawout circuit breakers to Ethernet networks via the Modbus TCP/IP protocol. It enables remote monitoring and data collection from the MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker and its MicroLogic X control unit. This DFB reads the MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker and its MicroLogic X control unit's data and presents it in the required format for use by the rest of the PLC program and/or by the HMI.

Input data mapping is based on the following document:
Name:		MasterPact MTZ – Modbus Communication (DOCA0105EN-10)
Version:		05/2023
FIlename:	DOCA0105EN-10.pdf

The following data will be read:
Address		Description				M580 IO Scanner Read Request
552 		Last Trip - Number of Alarm Causing Activation	1
553 		Last Trip - Trip Data &amp; Time			1
587		Last Trip - Phase A Current			2
589		Last Trip - Phase B Current			2
591 		Last Trip - Phase C Current			2
593 		Last Trip - Current on Neutral			2
24001 		Contact Wear Indicator (New = 0 1 = Replace)	3
32000 		Breaker Closed Data Valid			4
32000.2 		Breaker Fault Data Valid			4
32000.3 		Breaker Spring Loaded Data Valid		4
32000.5 		Breaker Ready to Close Data Valid		4
32001 		Breaker Closed				4
32001.2 		Breaker Fault				4
32001.3 		Breaker Spring Loaded			4
32001.5 		Breaker Ready to Close			4
32007 		Fault Status				4
32028 		RMS Current on Phase A			5
32030 		RMS Current on Phase B			5
32032 		RMS Current on Phase C			5
32034 		RMS Current on Neutral			5
32056 		RMS Phase A to B Voltage			6
32058 		RMS Phase B to C Voltage			6
32060 		RMS Phase C to A Voltage			6
32062 		RMS Phase A Voltage			6
32064 		RMS Phase B Voltage			6
32066 		RMS Phase C Voltage			6
32068 		Frequency				6
32078 		Total Active Power				6
32086 		Total Reactive Power			6
32094 		Total Apparent Power			6
32150 		Ground Fault Current			7
32164 		Total Active Power Demand			7
32166 		Total Reactive Power Demand			7
32168 		Total Apparent Power Demand		7
32212 		Total Power Factor				8
32222 		Phase A to B THD Voltage			8
32224 		Phase B to C THD Voltage			8
32226 		Phase C to A THD Voltage			8
32228 		Phase A THD Voltage			8
32230 		Phase B THD Voltage			8
32232 		Phase C THD Voltage			8
32234 		Phase A THD Current			8
32236 		Phase B THD Current			8
32238 		Phase C THD Current			8<objPosition posX="0" posY="11"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="6">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	07/07/2026	Initial Release<objPosition posX="0" posY="74"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="7">Communications to the circuit breaker are healthy when:
- the status of the communications module used is healthy
- the connection that is used to read data from the MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker is healthy.

When communications is unhealthy, all values read from the circuit breaker are invalid and set to zero.<objPosition posX="0" posY="81"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="6">The MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker is healthy when:
- Communications to the MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker (oDatOK) is healthy; AND
- Circuit breaker is not faulted (oCBFlt) and is valid data (oCBFltDatOK); AND
- Fault registers (FltSts1 &amp; FltSts2) are reporting healthy; AND
- Fault data validity registers (FltSts1OK &amp; FltSts2OK) are reporting all valid data.<objPosition posX="0" posY="191"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="5">The Communications fault (oComFlt) is active when:
- the connection that is used to read the data from the MasterPact MTZ circuit breaker is unhealthy; and
- both the status of the communications module (iPLMOK) and the power supply for the circuit breaker (iPwrOK) are healthy for 15s.
The delay is required to prevent the communication fault activating while the circuit breaker's starting up.<objPosition posX="0" posY="102"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="10">==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK - MasterPactMTZ
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Description:	      MasterPact MTZ Circuit Breaker
Date Changed:	      07/07/2026	
Change Comments:      Initial Release
Revision:	      1.00

==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2026
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="4">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
Status Mapping
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="133"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="4">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
Analogue Values Mapping
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="233"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
		<FBProgram name="Faults">
			<STSource>(* The tripping causes for the standard protection functions are split across 2 unsigned 16 bit registers with 1 = trip and not reset. The registers preceding them specifiy the validity of their signals *)



(* Create a string of the tripping causes for PLC display *)

IF NOT oDatOK THEN
	oFltTxt := 'Data invalid, no fault diagnostics to show';
	oSts.FltSts1 := 0;
	oSts.FltSts2 := 0;
ELSE
	oFltTxt := '';

	IF oSts.FltSts1.15 THEN
		oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Fault Word 1 Data invalid, ');
	ELSE
		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.0 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Long-Time Protection Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.0 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Long-Time Protection, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.1 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Short-Time Protection Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.1 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Short-Time Protection, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.2 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Instantaneous Protection Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.2 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Instantaneous Protection, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.3 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Ground-Fault Protection Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.3 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Ground-Fault Protection, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.4 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Earth-Leakage Protection Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.4 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Earth-Leakage Protection, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.5 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Integrated Instantaneous Protection Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.5 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Integrated Instantaneous Protection, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts1OK.6 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Internal Failure (Temperature) Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts1.6 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Internal Failure (Temperature), ');
		END_IF;
	END_IF;

	IF oSts.FltSts2.15 THEN
		oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Fault Word 2 Data invalid, ');

	ELSE
		IF NOT oSts.FltSts2OK.5 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Undervoltage Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts2.5 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Undervoltage, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts2OK.6 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Overvoltage Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts2.6 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Overvoltage, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts2OK.9 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Reverse Power Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts2.9 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Reverse Power, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts2OK.10 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Underfrequency Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts2.10 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Underfrequency, ');
		END_IF;

		IF NOT oSts.FltSts2OK.11 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Overfrequency Bit Invalid, ');
		ELSIF oSts.FltSts2.11 THEN
			oFltTxt := CONCAT_STR(oFltTxt, 'Overfrequency, ');
		END_IF;
	END_IF;

	IF oFltTxt = '' AND (oSts.FltSts1 &lt;&gt; 0 OR oSts.FltSts1OK &lt;&gt; 383 OR oSts.FltSts2 &lt;&gt; 0 OR oSts.FltSts2OK &lt;&gt; 3680) THEN
		oFltTxt := 'Unknown Fault Active, See Unit';
	ELSIF oFltTxt &lt;&gt; '' THEN
  		oFltTxt := REPLACE_INT(oFltTxt,'', 2, LEN_INT(oFltTxt)-1);
	ELSE
		oFltTxt := 'No Faults Active';
	END_IF;

END_IF;
</STSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
