					<textBox width="20" height="4">Capture Last Response Time
    <objPosition posX="83" posY="156"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="3">Check Watchdog for Change
===========================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="65"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="4">Update Watchdog history
    <objPosition posX="80" posY="85"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="3">Reset Statistics Conditions
===========================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="35"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="4">Capture Maximum Response Time
    <objPosition posX="120" posY="165"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="22" height="5">The time statistics are reset by the reset command.
    <objPosition posX="78" posY="38"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="3">Generate Success Counter Statistics
==============================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="235"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="3">Watchdog Timeout
===========================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="103"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="6">Detect if Watchdog changed, but only if non zero, to prevent communications failures (where input data is set to zero) being detected as a success
    <objPosition posX="80" posY="92"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="3">Generate Response Time Statistics
==============================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="145"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="4">Get Watchdog Register from Communications Data Array
    <objPosition posX="80" posY="70"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Description:
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
This DFB is intended for the monitoring of two communications channels that provide redundant communications to a remote device, using a primary and secondary communications channel, and passes the health channel’s communications input data to an output for use in the PLC code. If required, the block also provides heartbeat monitoring, and control outputs that may be used to enable the secondary channel upon failure of the primary.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="22" height="5">The counter statistics are reset either by the reset command, or when either counter is going to roll over.
    <objPosition posX="78" posY="49"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="4">Capture Cout of Successful Comms with Secondary
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="255"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="4">Capture Minimum Response Time
    <objPosition posX="120" posY="180"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="3">Determine the average communications update rate over 100 operations.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="195"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="22" height="11">Watchdog and Statistics Logic 
***********************************************
This logic determines the health of the Watchdog, and based on the Watchdog changes it determines the communications response time and communications statistics.

NOTE: This logic section is only solved when iWDEn is true.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="23"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="20" height="4">Capture Cout of Successful Comms with Primary
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="241"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="13">******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
 FUNCTION BLOCK - RdntCom
******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
 Description:              Redundant Communications
 Date Changed:         11/12/2019
 Change Comments:  DFB Created
 Revision:                   A

******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
 Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2019.
******************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="40" height="5">Raise timeout if the Watchdog does not change within timeout delay. Only time when either of the communicaitons channels is healthy.  Once faulted, wait a number of transactions before returning to healthy.
    <objPosition posX="80" posY="103"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
