					<textBox width="90" height="3">On a change of shift, move the shift totaliser into the previous shift total.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="85"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="13">==============================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK		TotaliserPulse
==============================================================================================================================================================
Description:		Totalise a Digital Input Totaliser Pulse
Date Changed:		25/07/2020
Change Comments:	Initial Release
Revision:		1.00

==============================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2020
==============================================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Increment the shift totaliser value by the pulse difference.
On a change of shift or reset request, reset the shift totaliser to zero.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="174"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Determine the change in the totaliser based on a new pulse.
Track the REAL number rollover value to prevent accumulating errors.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="134"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="10">Revision History
==============================================================================================================================================================
1.00	NJA	25/07/2020	Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="50"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Store the current pulse value for next PLC scan.
If the pulse value goes unhealthy, do not update the last value to prevent invalid pulses on healthy data.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="194"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">The shift totals are reset on the rising edge of the shift reset input pin.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="65"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="5">Increment the main totaliser value by the pulse difference.
Roll the totaliser value over at 999,999,999 to prevent PLC overflow errors.
On a reset pulse, reset the main totaliser.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="153"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="35">Description:
==============================================================================================================================================================
The DFB takes a pulse signal input and accumulates a pre-defined quantity every pulse in an output total value. It also tracks the total accumulated value per shift, and stores this value to a previous shift total whenever a shift reset pulse input is received.

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
   •  Receive a pulse signal which is used to trigger a totaliser accumulation.
   •  Use a quantity per pulse input constant to add to an absolute total whenever a pulse signal is received.
   •  Use a quantity per pulse input constant to add to a shift total whenever a pulse signal is received.
   •  Incorporate “roll-over” logic for the absolute total accumulator to prevent overflow if the total is very large.
   •  Track rounding errors when accumulating REAL quantity per pulse into the DINT totaliser to ensure that they are included in the next calculation.
   •  Save the current shift total into a previous shift total when receiving shift reset pulse.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Detect valid totaliser update pulses.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="105"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
