						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<textBox width="80" height="35">Description:
==============================================================================================================================================================
The DFB takes a pulse signal input and accumulates a pre-defined quantity every pulse into differing statistical output total values.

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
   •  Receive a pulse signal which is used to trigger a totaliser accumulation.
   •  Use a quantity per pulse input constant to add to an absolute total whenever a pulse signal is received.
   •  Use a quantity per pulse input constant to add to a shift total whenever a pulse signal is received.
   •  Incorporate “roll-over” logic for the master total accumulator to prevent overflow if the total is very large.
   • Track rounding errors when accumulating REAL quantity per pulse into the DINT totaliser to ensure that they are included in the next calculation.
   • Save the current statistic totals to previous statistic totals when receiving statistic reset pulse.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="10">Revision History
==============================================================================================================================================================
1.01	MBT	11/03/2025	Application of Totaliser Scaling Factor
1.00	MBT	12/07/2024	Initial Release - update of TotaliserPulse
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="50"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Day Totaliser
===============
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="231"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="3">On a change of shift, move the shift totaliser into the previous shift total and reset this shift value.
    <objPosition posX="20" posY="205"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="28" height="3">Roll the totaliser value over at 999,999,999 to prevent any errors.
On a reset pulse, reset the main totaliser.
    <objPosition posX="60" posY="185"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Master Totaliser
===============
Condition the Master Totaliser Scaling Factor such that at a minimum the scaling factor is 1
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="172"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Determine the change in the totaliser based on a new pulse.
Track the REAL number rollover value to prevent accumulating errors.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="134"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">The statistic totals are reset on the rising edge of the corresponding reset pulse.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="65"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="13">==============================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK		TotaliserPulseStat_V2
==============================================================================================================================================================
Description:		Totalise a Digital Input Totaliser Pulse into Reporting Statistics
Date Changed:		11/03/2025
Change Comments:	Addition of master totaliser scaling factor
Revision:		1.01

==============================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2020
==============================================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="3">On a change of month, move the month totaliser into the previous month total and reset this month value.
    <objPosition posX="20" posY="295"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="4">Store the current pulse value for next PLC scan.
If the pulse value goes unhealthy, do not update the last value to prevent invalid pulses on healthy data.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="154"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Month Totaliser
===============
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="291"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="3">On a change of day, move the day totaliser into the previous day total and reset this day value.
    <objPosition posX="20" posY="235"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Capture the pulse update type.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="95"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="3">On a change of week, move the week totaliser into the previous week total and reset this week value.
    <objPosition posX="20" posY="265"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="28" height="3">Apply any scaling factor for the master totaliser (i.e. to go from L to kL, scale by 1000)
    <objPosition posX="25" posY="185"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Shift Totaliser
===============
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="201"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="90" height="3">Week Totaliser
===============
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="261"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
