					</linkFB>
					<linkFB>
						<linkSource parentObjectName="R_Trig_Stt" pinName="Q">
							<objPosition posX="13" posY="26"></objPosition>
						</linkSource>
						<linkDestination parentObjectName=".35" pinName="IN1">
							<objPosition posX="21" posY="26"></objPosition>
						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<linkFB>
						<linkSource parentObjectName=".36" pinName="OUT">
							<objPosition posX="38" posY="26"></objPosition>
						</linkSource>
						<linkDestination parentObjectName=".12" pinName="IN1">
							<objPosition posX="44" posY="26"></objPosition>
						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<textBox width="99" height="5">The oTstDet output is set ON when: 
The equipment is in the required mode for the test and the test is started (eg: by pushbutton in the field), while iTstCndRdy (eg: CB open AND PLC I/O modules healthy etc) is ON.
Note that the Isolation Work Practice details the necessary steps to achieve a safe working environment, and the output of the DFB must not be used as a guarantee that the equipment has been correctly isolated according to the Isolation Work Practice.
    <objPosition posX="1" posY="15"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
