					<textBox width="106" height="7">Latched Limit Status
=================
When iHld is OFF indicating that the Open &amp; Close outputs are pulse outputs and iLmtFltTm is greater than zero indicating Fail to Open/Close faults require the limits to be off for a certain time then there is a possibility that the Outputs will cycle ON &amp; OFF if the limits are bouncing on and off. Therefore when the limits are achieved in this mode the signals are latched preventing cycling of the outputs. The Fail to Open/Close faults should trip the valve if required via the interlocks.
Additionally when the valve has reached it's required opened or closed state this latched status is used to detect any limit position failures.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="289"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="13">VALVE CONTROL
==============
There are two states for the valve: Open or Close and these states can be output to one output or two output depending on the valve itself. 
For valves with one output, only use the oOpn. 
For valves with two outputs, use both oOpn and oCls.

For mode selection, there are three options depending if the valve has local control: Auto, Manual or Local (if valve has local control).
The position of the valve will stay the same when the mode of the valve is changed from one to another, unless the switch is already in an open or a close position in local mode.

The valve may or may not have limit switches.
If there is no limit switches, then feed the oOpn and oCls to iOpnLmt and iClsLmt respectively.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="12"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="18" height="4">Initiate a Auto Close if the Sequence Close is requested and the start interlocks are healthy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="167"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="18" height="4">Initiate a Auto Open if the Sequence Open is requested and the start interlocks are healthy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="150"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="106" height="8">Auto Control Seal
===============
The valve may be placed in auto mode via the group auto command or the auto button for each individual valve in the HMI.
The valve will open/close if the sequence initial open/close and sequence open/close interlocks are OK and the fault seal is not true.

In the event that both Sequence interlocks are true, the valve will failsafe to the position specified in iFSPos.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="140"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="106" height="4">Valve Outputs
===============
The valve will open/close if the open/close seal are satisfied or if the fault seal is on, then the valve will failsafe to the state defined by iFSPos.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="259"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="4">Valve Modes
===========
When PLC starts, Manual mode is the default mode unless another mode is selected in its initialisation.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="52"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="106" height="5">Manual Control Seal
================
The valve may be placed in manual mode by clicking the manual button for each individual valve in HMI.
The valve will operate in manual mode if its fault seal is not true.
I
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="184"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="11" height="2">Open Output
    <objPosition posX="76" posY="266"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="9">If the valve is auto open requested and the sequence open is still active however the sequence close start and request are active and the default position is closed then reset the auto open request. 
i.e. Valve wants to close but Sequence Open is still on.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="157"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="106" height="5">Local Control Seal (if valve has local control)
=====================================
The valve may be placed in local mode via the local button for each individual valve in the HMI.
The valve will open/close by using the the local control and it will operate if the trip interlocks are healty.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="222"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="8" height="2">Fault Latch
    <objPosition posX="46" posY="99"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Manual Close Seal
    <objPosition posX="46" posY="207"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="19" height="9">If the valve is auto close requested and the sequence close is still active however the sequence open start and request are active and the default position is open then reset the auto close request. 
i.e. Valve wants to open but Sequence Close is still on.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="174"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="8" height="2">Auto Ready
    <objPosition posX="66" posY="98"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="8" height="2">Reset Required
    <objPosition posX="66" posY="109"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Local Close Seal
    <objPosition posX="46" posY="244"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="11" height="2">Close Output
    <objPosition posX="76" posY="277"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Manual Open Seal
    <objPosition posX="46" posY="191"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Local Open Seal
    <objPosition posX="46" posY="229"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Fault Acknowledge
================
In Auto or Manual mode the operator will acknowledge the fault from the HM.
In Local and Out of Service mode the fault is automatically reset.
The oFltRst output shall be used to reset all alarms associate with the valve.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="118"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Auto Close Seal
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="167"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="3">Unpack HMI Command Word
=======================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="26"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="11" height="2">Opened Latched Status
    <objPosition posX="36" posY="298"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="11" height="2">Closed Latched Status
    <objPosition posX="76" posY="298"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="7">Fault Seal &amp; Reset Required
=======================
The fault seal self latches whenever the valve faults in Auto mode or a critical interlock faults in Local mode.
In Auto or Manual mode once the fault has been cleared the Reset Required status will become healthy indicating to the controller that a fault acknowledge from the HMI is required to unlatch the Fault Seal.
In Local mode the fault will reset automatically when the fault has been cleared.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="89"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="10" height="2">Auto Open Seal
    <objPosition posX="56" posY="150"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
