					<textBox width="100" height="2">Map UPS status register for decoding and generate UPS statuses from it<objPosition posX="10" posY="105"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="10">UPS healthy when:
- Data read back from the CS141 BACS Webmanager unit is healthy;
- UPS system is normal and output is on;
- UPS bypass is inactive;
- UPS output is not overloaded;
- UPS general fault status is inactive;
- UPS communications fault status is inactive; and
- UPS alarm registers are reporting 0.<objPosition posX="10" posY="137"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="26">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
The Generex CS141 unit is a universal UPS management adapter used to monitor and manage uninterruptible power supplies. The CS141 Battery Analysis &amp; Care Systems (BACS) Webmanager unit is a specialized version of the base CS141 unit. While it still monitors the UPS, it includes firmware and a hardware interface designed to monitor individual battery health (voltage, temperature, and internal resistance) in real-time. The CS141 BACS Webmanager unit communicates via Modbus TCP. This DFB reads the ABB UPScale UPS and BACS data and presents it in the required format for use by the rest of the PLC program and/or by the HMI.

The Brockman Syncline 1 (BS1) greenfields substations, BSR130, BSR131 and BSR132 have the following BACS module arrangement:
BSR130UP01 3 strings of 40
BSR131 &amp; BSR132 UP01 2 strings of 40

This DFB allows for up to 2 strings of 40 BACS modules, use the UPScale_CS141_BSR130 DFB for BSR130UP01.

Input data mapping is based on the following document:
Name:		GENEREX Comprehensive User Manuals
Version:		v.2025-09-18 FW2.16-2.26
FIlename:	manual_CS141_en incl modbus

The following data will be read:
UPS - ABB/NEWAVE UPS Type Concept Power (Addresses 100 - 183)
BACS System - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1000 - 1005)
BACS String 1 - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1010 - 1013)
BACS String 2 - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1015 - 1018)
BACS Modules 1 - 80 - BACS MODBUS Parameter (Addresses 1060 - 1459)<objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="13">==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK - UPScale_CS141
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Description:	      ABB UPScale CS141 BACS Webmanager
Date Changed:	      09/07/2026	
Change Comments:      Initial Release
Revision:	      1.00

==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2026
==========================================================================================================================================================================================================================<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="4">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
UPS Status Mapping
****************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="100"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="7">Communications to the CS141 BACS Webmanager unit are healthy when:
- the status of the communications module used is healthy
- the connection that is used to read data from the CS141 BACS Webmanager unit is healthy.

When communications is unhealthy, all values read from the unit are invalid and set to zero.<objPosition posX="0" posY="51"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="5">The Communications fault (oComFlt) is active when:
- the connection that is used to read the data from the CS141 BACS Webmanager unit is unhealthy; and
- both the status of the communications module (iPLMOK) and the power supply for the unit (iPwrOK) are healthy for 15s.
The delay is required to prevent the communication fault activating while the unit's starting up.<objPosition posX="0" posY="72"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="110" height="9">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	09/07/2026	Initial Release<objPosition posX="0" posY="41"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
