						<linkSource parentObjectName=".12" pinName="OUT">
							<objPosition posX="39" posY="122"></objPosition>
						</linkSource>
						<linkDestination parentObjectName=".8" pinName="IN1">
							<objPosition posX="44" posY="122"></objPosition>
						</linkDestination>
					</linkFB>
					<textBox width="100" height="13">Description
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
This DFB can be used to generate fault conditions of: High High, High, Low and Low Low from input Value for comparison

The user is able to set real value setpoints (iLoLoSP, iLoSP, iHiSP &amp; iHiHiSP) for each of these conditions, which defines when they are latched. 
No check is made that the relative value of the setpoints matches their names
e.g. the High-High setpoint value could be less than the High setpoint value and the block would still function correctly.
The DFB also accepts the hysteresis value (iHys) which is a positve number common to all four conditions and defines when the points are unlatched.<objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="3">iHys is limited between 0 and its own value to prevent it being set to a negative value.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="31"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="10">This section determines when to latch the HiHi, Hi, Lo and LoLo Conditions and when to unlatch them.

The Hi and HiHi Conditions latch when the input Value is greater than or equal to the setpoint and unlatch when it is below the setpoint minus the hystersis value.

The Lo &amp; LoLo Conditions latch when the input Value is less than or equal to the setpoint and unlatch when it is greater than the setpoint plus the hysteresis value.<objPosition posX="0" posY="45"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="12">*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  FUNCTION BLOCK - ValComp
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Description:              Value Compare
  Change Comments:  Adapted from B4 &amp; HD4 ValComp DFB and CLB KP_Setpoint.

*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
  Copyright Rio Tinto Pty Ltd, 2019.
*********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
	<FBSource nameOfFBType="ValFrz" version="0.60" dateTime="dt#2019-11-11-17:00:07">
		<comment>Value Frozen</comment>
