					<textBox width="13" height="2">Arc Flash Protection Fault
    <objPosition posX="4" posY="109"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="13" height="2">System Fault
    <objPosition posX="33" posY="109"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="13">==========================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK - VAMP321
==========================================================================================================================================
Description:		Schneider Electric VAMP 321 Arc Flash Protection
Date Changed:		10/02/2026
Change Comments:	Fixed DFB intro comments and standardized comment box lengths
Revision:			1.02

==========================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2026
==========================================================================================================================================<objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="5">The Module fault (oFlt) is active when:
- the connection that is used to read the data from the COM35 Module is unhealthy; and
- both the status of the communications module (iPLMOK) and the power supply for the unit (iPwrOK) are healthy for 15s.
The delay is required to prevent the communication fault activating while the unit's starting up.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="63"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="5">***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
Fault Bit Mapping
***************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="93"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="15">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================
DFB Reference Document Number: KD-0061-J-SPE-00062

Introduction: The VAMP321_In DFB is used to interface with a Schneider Electric VAMP 321 Arc Flash Protection device, used in arc flash protection applications for low or medium voltage power distribution systems. The device is intended to be used in combination with arc flash protection I/O units and sensors.<objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="13" height="2">Move into DDT
    <objPosition posX="12" posY="196"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="13" height="4">Bit 0 = Output Relay 1 - Configured as Arc Flash Protection Fault (detected)
    <objPosition posX="7" posY="120"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="13" height="4">OR all bits from 4 Diagnostics Registers to give an overall System Fault
    <objPosition posX="52" posY="125"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="7">Communications to the unit are healthy when:
- the status of the communications module used is healthy
- the connection that is used to read data from the Module is healthy.

When communications is unhealthy, all values read from the unit are invalid and set to zero.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="41"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="10">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.02	BCY	10/02/2024		Fixed DFB intro comments and standardized comment box lengths
1.01	CH	26/02/2024		oProFlt bit updated from iDatIn1.0 to iDatIn1.1
1.00	AXY	12/10/2022		Initial Release based on GD1<objPosition posX="0" posY="30"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
