					<textBox width="120" height="3">Map out the fault status byte for module condition masking.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="109"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="22" height="15">HART module status diagnostics
Bit 1: Disconnected (=1 if any channel is in the disconnected state)

Bit 2: Instrument Changed, Minor (=1 if any channel is in the instrument changed, minor state)

Bit 3: Instrument Changed, Major (=1 if any channel is in the instrument changed, major state)

Bit 7: ICE (=1 on the occurrence of an internal communication event)
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="195"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="9">Revision History
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	25/10/2023		Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="77"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="13">==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK -	X80_AHI0812In
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Description:		X80 BME AHI0812 8 Channel HART Analogue Input Module Diagnostics &amp; Mapping
Date Changed:		25/10/2023
Change Comments:	Initial Release
Revision:		1.00

==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2023
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="7">Communication to the unit is healthy when status of the communications module used is healthy after delay.
The CPU FDR server will automatically reupload DTM configurations to the AHI0812 module upon either:
- replacing a module
- re-establishing PLC communications to the CRA module
A delay is required to allow DTM configuration transfer to occur, preventing 'Config Fault' displaying before transfer has completed.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="87"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="2">Map out the module diagnostic bits for HMI display.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="161"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="4">The module status is healthy (oOK) provided:
- The associated network module (iLnkOK) is healthy; AND
- The module is not reporting any non-channel related faults.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="129"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="62">Description:
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
This DFB is used to unmap the input data from a BME AHI0812 8 Channel HART Analogue Input module to monitor the input analogue values, the module and channel statuses and the HART diagnostics.

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
• Generate a module healthy output (oOK) when the module is healthy;
• Generate channel healthy outputs (oCh0OK – oCh7OK) for each healthy channel;
• Generate a module fault output (oFlt) when the module is unhealthy;
• Generate channel fault outputs (oCh0Flt – oCh7Flt) for each unhealthy channel; 
• Mask the module health based on the associated network module health (iLnkOK) status;
• Mask channel health (oCh0OK – oCh7OK) and fault (oCh0Flt – oCh7Flt) statuses based on the module health (oOK) status;
• Map the channel hold values (iCh0HldVal - iCh7HldVal) to analogue input channels (oCh0PV – oCh7PV) for unhealthy channels;
• Detect channel under current and over current faults; and
• Read the HART diagnostics from the process instrument.

The BME AHI0812 module requires the following CPU Ethernet port Security settings:
CPU EIO -&gt; Security
      • FTP - Enabled
      • TFTP - Enabled
      • DHCP / BOOTP - Enabled
      • EIP - Enabled

The BME AHI0812 module requires the following DTM Address Settings:
CPU DTM -&gt; Device List -&gt; BME AHI0812 module -&gt; Address Server -&gt; Identifier.
If module is on the main local rack:
      • Mx80_yy_&lt;module&gt;
Where yy = slot number and &lt;module&gt; is the module mnemonic. E.g. Identifier linking AHI card in slot 2 of a main rack = Mx80_02_AHI0812
OR
If module is on a remote IO rack:
      • Cxxx_yy_&lt;module&gt;
Where Cxxx = Drop number, yy = slot number and &lt;module&gt; is the module mnemonic. E.g. Identifier linking AHI card in drop 4 slot 6 = C004_06_AHI0812.

The BME AHI0812 module DTM must be configured to make all of its Process Data available for reading.

Each channel of the BME AHI0812 module must be configured as follows in the module configuration:
  USED – The channel must be enabled or the DFB will set the channel unhealthy and mask its fault status.
  RANGE - Defines the analogue input range. The BME AHI0812 module only works with the 4-20mA range
  SCALE - Defines the measurement parameters of the channel:
      • Scaling Range - Must be configured with the following values as they are hard coded in the DFB:
            0%-&gt;       0,000
            100%-&gt;    10,000
      • Overflow - These values are used by the DFB for over/under current detection. Recommended (default) values are as follows (4-20mA):
            Below:      -800
              Checked   Yes
            Above:    10,800
              Checked   Yes
      A measurement beyond the Overflow value will fault the channel.
  FILTER - Defines the level of first order filtering for a channel. Recommended (default) value is 0.

This DFB is designed to work with an associated X80_AHI0812Out DFB.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="4">The module fault (oFlt) is active when:
- The associated network module (iLnkOK) is healthy; AND
- The module is reporting a non-channel related fault.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="149"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
