					<textBox width="130" height="3">Map the process value to the DFB output.
Note: The TRUE_VALUE is used to prevent mapping of the forced value of the input channel. This is required as the forced state of the channel is not easily visible in the DDT.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="198"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="7">The channel is healthy (oChxOK) provided:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- The channel (ChxEn) is enabled in the module configuration; AND
- The channel is reporting healthy.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="336"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="8">The channel under / over current error (oChxUCE / oChxOCE) is active 
when:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- The channel (oChxOK) is reporting unhealthy; AND
- The analogue input measurement is within the lower / upper tolerance zone as defined in the module configuration.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="217"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="5">Map out the:
- raw channel health for HMI display; AND
- the channel enabled status (FCT_TYPE = 1) in the module configuration.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="170"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="140" height="3">Channel 5
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="325"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="8">The channel under / over current error (oChxUCE / oChxOCE) is active 
when:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- The channel (oChxOK) is reporting unhealthy; AND
- The analogue input measurement is within the lower / upper tolerance zone as defined in the module configuration.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="377"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="13">The power supply module maintains power to the rack for up to 500ms after total power loss. During this time, the IO module produces channel faults due to loss of loop power. 

A delay is required to mask the Channel Fault (oChxFlt).

A Channel Fault status (oChxFlt) is latched (ChxFltSL) upon detecting a channel fault. This guarantees a fault will occur as long as the Module Health (oOK) is not lost within 600ms and ensures that faults which only occur for a single scan can be captured and alarmed outside the DFB.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="184"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="130" height="3">Map the process value to the DFB output.
Note: The TRUE_VALUE is used to prevent mapping of the forced value of the input channel. This is required as the forced state of the channel is not easily visible in the DDT.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="38"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="8">The channel under / over current error (oChxUCE / oChxOCE) is active 
when:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- The channel (oChxOK) is reporting unhealthy; AND
- The analogue input measurement is within the lower / upper tolerance zone as defined in the module configuration.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="57"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="40" height="22">HART channel status diagnostics (Numbers are value, not bit number)
0: CH-Disabled (The channel is disabled)

1: CH-Connecting (The module is searching for, and attempting to connect with, a HART instrument on the channel)

2: CH-Connected (The channel is connected to a HART instrument)

3: CH-MinorDiff (One or more minor differences exist between the connected HART instrument and the instrument description in the multiplexer island configuration)

4: CH-MajorDiff (One or more major differences exist between the connected HART instrument and the instrument description in the multiplexer island configuration)

5: CH-Disconnected (This state indicates either the module discovered no HART instrument on the channel after performing 2 scans of the specified address range OR the module discovered a HART instrument on the channel, but the connection was lost. The module continues to search for a HART instrument on this channel)
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="94"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="40" height="22">HART channel status diagnostics (Numbers are value, not bit number)
0: CH-Disabled (The channel is disabled)

1: CH-Connecting (The module is searching for, and attempting to connect with, a HART instrument on the channel)

2: CH-Connected (The channel is connected to a HART instrument)

3: CH-MinorDiff (One or more minor differences exist between the connected HART instrument and the instrument description in the multiplexer island configuration)

4: CH-MajorDiff (One or more major differences exist between the connected HART instrument and the instrument description in the multiplexer island configuration)

5: CH-Disconnected (This state indicates either the module discovered no HART instrument on the channel after performing 2 scans of the specified address range OR the module discovered a HART instrument on the channel, but the connection was lost. The module continues to search for a HART instrument on this channel)
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="254"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="7">The channel is healthy (oChxOK) provided:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- The channel (ChxEn) is enabled in the module configuration; AND
- The channel is reporting healthy.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="16"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="43" height="25">HART instrument status diagnostics
Bit 0: Primary variable out of limits: the value of the instrument Primary Variable (PV) has traveled beyond its operating limits

Bit 1: Non-primary variable out of limits: the value of an instrument variable, other than the Primary Variable (PV), has traveled beyond its operating limits

Bit 2: Loop current saturated: current on the HART channel has reached its upper or lower limit, and cannot increase or decrease further

Bit 3: Loop current fixed: current on the HART channel is being held at a fixed value, and is not responding to process variations

Bit 4: More status available: additional instrument information is available via HART command 48 (Read Additional Status Information)

Bit 5: Cold start: the instrument was reset, or power was cycled off then on

Bit 6: Configuration changed: an operation occurred that changed the instrument configuration

Bit 7: Device malfunction: a detected error rendered the instrument non-operational
    <objPosition posX="77" posY="288"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="43" height="25">HART instrument status diagnostics
Bit 0: Primary variable out of limits: the value of the instrument Primary Variable (PV) has traveled beyond its operating limits

Bit 1: Non-primary variable out of limits: the value of an instrument variable, other than the Primary Variable (PV), has traveled beyond its operating limits

Bit 2: Loop current saturated: current on the HART channel has reached its upper or lower limit, and cannot increase or decrease further

Bit 3: Loop current fixed: current on the HART channel is being held at a fixed value, and is not responding to process variations

Bit 4: More status available: additional instrument information is available via HART command 48 (Read Additional Status Information)

Bit 5: Cold start: the instrument was reset, or power was cycled off then on

Bit 6: Configuration changed: an operation occurred that changed the instrument configuration

Bit 7: Device malfunction: a detected error rendered the instrument non-operational
    <objPosition posX="77" posY="128"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="5">Map out the:
- raw channel health for HMI display; AND
- the channel enabled status (FCT_TYPE = 1) in the module configuration.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="10"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="40" height="22">HART channel status diagnostics (Numbers are value, not bit number)
0: CH-Disabled (The channel is disabled)

1: CH-Connecting (The module is searching for, and attempting to connect with, a HART instrument on the channel)

2: CH-Connected (The channel is connected to a HART instrument)

3: CH-MinorDiff (One or more minor differences exist between the connected HART instrument and the instrument description in the multiplexer island configuration)

4: CH-MajorDiff (One or more major differences exist between the connected HART instrument and the instrument description in the multiplexer island configuration)

5: CH-Disconnected (This state indicates either the module discovered no HART instrument on the channel after performing 2 scans of the specified address range OR the module discovered a HART instrument on the channel, but the connection was lost. The module continues to search for a HART instrument on this channel)
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="414"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="13">The power supply module maintains power to the rack for up to 500ms after total power loss. During this time, the IO module produces channel faults due to loss of loop power. 

A delay is required to mask the Channel Fault (oChxFlt).

A Channel Fault status (oChxFlt) is latched (ChxFltSL) upon detecting a channel fault. This guarantees a fault will occur as long as the Module Health (oOK) is not lost within 600ms and ensures that faults which only occur for a single scan can be captured and alarmed outside the DFB.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="344"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="140" height="3">Channel 4
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="165"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="140" height="3">Channel 3
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="5"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="13">The power supply module maintains power to the rack for up to 500ms after total power loss. During this time, the IO module produces channel faults due to loss of loop power. 

A delay is required to mask the Channel Fault (oChxFlt).

A Channel Fault status (oChxFlt) is latched (ChxFltSL) upon detecting a channel fault. This guarantees a fault will occur as long as the Module Health (oOK) is not lost within 600ms and ensures that faults which only occur for a single scan can be captured and alarmed outside the DFB.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="24"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="30" height="7">The channel is healthy (oChxOK) provided:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- The channel (ChxEn) is enabled in the module configuration; AND
- The channel is reporting healthy.
    <objPosition posX="70" posY="176"></objPosition>
