					<textBox width="43" height="25">HART instrument status diagnostics
Bit 0: Primary variable out of limits: the value of the instrument Primary Variable (PV) has traveled beyond its operating limits

Bit 1: Non-primary variable out of limits: the value of an instrument variable, other than the Primary Variable (PV), has traveled beyond its operating limits

Bit 2: Loop current saturated: current on the HART channel has reached its upper or lower limit, and cannot increase or decrease further

Bit 3: Loop current fixed: current on the HART channel is being held at a fixed value, and is not responding to process variations

Bit 4: More status available: additional instrument information is available via HART command 48 (Read Additional Status Information)

Bit 5: Cold start: the instrument was reset, or power was cycled off then on

Bit 6: Configuration changed: an operation occurred that changed the instrument configuration

Bit 7: Device malfunction: a detected error rendered the instrument non-operational
    <objPosition posX="77" posY="448"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="130" height="3">Map the process value to the DFB output.
Note: The TRUE_VALUE is used to prevent mapping of the forced value of the input channel. This is required as the forced state of the channel is not easily visible in the DDT.
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="358"></objPosition>
