					<textBox width="120" height="2">Map out the module diagnostic bits for HMI display.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="136"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="4">The module fault (oFlt) is active when:
- The associated network module (iLnkOK) is healthy; AND
- The module is reporting a non-channel related fault.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="124"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="3">Map out the fault status byte for module condition masking.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="85"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="13">==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK -	X80_AHO0412In
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Description:		X80 BME AHO0412 4 Channel HART Analogue Output Module Diagnostics
Date Changed:		26/5/2023
Change Comments:	Initial Release
Revision:		1.00

==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2023
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="22" height="15">HART module status diagnostics
Bit 1: Disconnected (=1 if any channel is in the disconnected state)

Bit 2: Instrument Changed, Minor (=1 if any channel is in the instrument changed, minor state)

Bit 3: Instrument Changed, Major (=1 if any channel is in the instrument changed, major state)

Bit 7: ICE (=1 on the occurrence of an internal communication event)
    <objPosition posX="10" posY="170"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="60">Description:
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
This DFB is used to unmap the input data from a BME AHO0412 4 Channel HART Analogue Output module to monitor the module and channel statuses and the HART diagnostics.

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
• Generate a module healthy output (oOK) when the module is healthy;
• Generate channel healthy outputs (oCh0OK – oCh3OK) for each healthy channel;
• Generate a module fault output (oFlt) when the module is unhealthy;
• Generate channel fault outputs (oCh0Flt – oCh3Flt) for each unhealthy channel; 
• Mask the module health based on the associated network module health (iLnkOK) status;
• Mask channel health (oCh0OK – oCh3OK) and fault (oCh0Flt – oCh3Flt) statuses based on the module health (oOK) status; and
• Read the HART diagnostics from the process instrument.

The BME AHO0412 module requires the following CPU Ethernet port Security settings:
CPU EIO -&gt; Security
      • FTP - Enabled
      • TFTP - Enabled
      • DHCP / BOOTP - Enabled
      • EIP - Enabled

The BME AHO0412 module requires the following DTM Address Settings:
CPU DTM -&gt; Device List -&gt; BME AHO0412 module -&gt; Address Server -&gt; Identifier.
If module is on the main local rack:
      • Mx80_yy_&lt;module&gt;
Where yy = slot number and &lt;module&gt; is the module mnemonic. E.g. Identifier linking AHO card in slot 2 of a main rack = Mx80_02_AHO0412
OR
If module is on a remote IO rack:
      • Cxxx_yy_&lt;module&gt;
Where Cxxx = Drop number, yy = slot number and &lt;module&gt; is the module mnemonic. E.g. Identifier linking AHO card in drop 4 slot 6 = C004_06_AHO0412.

The BME AHO0412 module DTM must be configured to make all of its Process Data available for reading.

Each channel of the BME AHO0412 module must be configured as follows in the module configuration:
  RANGE - Defines the analogue input range. The BME AHO0412 module only works with the 4-20mA range
  SCALE - Defines the measurement parameters of the channel:
      • Scaling Range - Must be configured with the following values as they are hard coded in the DFB:
            0%-&gt;       0,000
            100%-&gt;    10,000
      • Overflow - These values are used by the DFB for over/under current detection. Recommended (default) values are as follows (4-20mA):
            Below:      -800
              Checked   Yes
            Above:    10,300
              Checked   Yes
      A measurement beyond the Overflow value will fault the channel.
  FALLBACK - Specifies the behavior of the output when the PLC is in STOP mode or if communication between the PLC and the output module has stopped. Recommended (default) value is on / checked.
  FALLBACK VALUE - Defines the fallback value of the channel. Recommended (default) value is "0".
  WIRING CTRL - Controls whether the wiring control function, which checks for a broken wire, is on or off. Recommended value is on / checked.

This DFB is designed to work with an associated X80_AHO0412Out DFB.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="4">The module status is healthy (oOK) provided:
- The associated network module (iLnkOK) is healthy; AND
- The module is not reporting any non-channel related faults.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="104"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="120" height="9">Revision History
==============================================================================================================================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	26/5/2023	Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="75"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
