					<textBox width="80" height="13">==============================================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK -	X80_DDI3202K
==============================================================================================================================================================
Description:		X80 BMX DDI3202K 32 Channel Digital Input Module Diagnostics &amp; Mapping	
Date Changed:		02/04/2020
Change Comments:	Initial Release
Revision:		1.00

==============================================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2020
==============================================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="10">Revision History
==============================================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	02/04/2020	Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="50"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">The module fault (oFlt) is active when:
- The CRA module island healthy (iLnkOK) status is active; AND
- The module is reporting a non-channel related fault.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="103"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">Each channel group status is healthy (oGrp1OK &amp; oGrp2OK) provided:
- The module (oOK) is reporting healthy; AND
- All channels within the group are healthy.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="124"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="100" height="2">Map out the module diagnostic bits for HMI display.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="276"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="4">The module status is healthy (oOK) provided:
- The CRA module island healthy (iLnkOK) status is active; AND
- The module is not reporting any non-channel related faults.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="84"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="3">Map out the digital input channels to a DWORD. The DWORD can be mapped into individual channels outside the DFB. Individual channels cannot be outputted from the DFB as Unity Pro limits the number of output pins to 32.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="225"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="35">Description:
==============================================================================================================================================================
This DFB is used to unmap the input data from a X80 BMX DDI3202K 32 Channel Digital Input module to monitor the module and channel group health statuses.

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
• Generate a module healthy output (oOK) if the module is healthy; 
• Generate channel group healthy outputs (oGrp1OK &amp; oGrp2OK) if each channel group is healthy;
• Generate a module fault output (oFlt) if the module is unhealthy;
• Generate channel group fault outputs (oGrp1Flt &amp; oGrp2Flt) if each channel group is unhealthy; 
• Mask the module health based on the CRA module health (iLnkOK) status;
• Mask channel group health (oGrp1OK &amp; oGrp2OK) and fault (oGrp1Flt &amp; oGrp2Flt) statuses based on the module healthy (oOK) status;
• Mask digital input channel values (oDat) based on the module healthy (oOK) and channel group health (oGrp1OK &amp; oGrp2OK) statuses; and
• Output the channel data (oDat) as a packed DWORD as Unity Pro limits the number of output pins on a DFB to 32. The DWORD can be mapped into individual channels outside the DFB. It is recommended to use the Unpack32 DFB for this purpose.

The BMX DDI3202K module must have the following parameters configured:
SUPPLY MONITORING - Enables power supply monitoring function for each group of 16 channels. It is enabled by default.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="2">Map out the fault status byte for diagnostics
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="66"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="80" height="7">The CPS module maintains power to the rack for up to 600ms after total power loss. During this time, the IO module produces channel group faults due to loss of loop power. A delay is required to mask the Channel Group Fault (oGrpxFlt).

A Channel Group Fault status (oGrpxFlt) is latched (Grp1FltSL) upon detecting a channel group fault. This guarantees a fault will occur as long as the Module Health (oOK) is not lost within 600ms and ensures that faults which only occur for a single scan can be captured and alarmed outside the DFB.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="181"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
