					<textBox width="70" height="5">The module fault (oFlt) is active when:
- The CRA network module (iLnkOK) is healthy; AND
- The module is reporting unhealthy.
Note: The MOD_HEALTH is a global health status and includes all fault statuses in MOD_FLT.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="113"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="45">Description:
==============================================================================================================================================================
This DFB is used to unmap the status data from a X80 BMX DDO1602 16 Channel Digital Output module to monitor the module health and channel error statuses. 

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
• Generate a module healthy output (oOK) if the module is healthy; 
• Generate a module fault output (oFlt) if the module is unhealthy;
• Generate a channel error word output (oSts.ChErr) to track if each channel is unhealthy; and
• Mask the module health and channel error word based on the CRA network health (iLnkOK) status. 

The BMX DDO1602 module must have the following parameters set:
SUPPLY MONITORING - Sets the power supply monitoring function for the 16 channels on or off. It is enabled by default.

REACTIVATE - Defines the reactivation mode of outputs tripped by overloads or short-circuits. The options available are as follows:
  • Programmed	- Do not use.
  • Automatic	- Select.

FALLBACK MODE - Defines the fallback mode adopted by outputs when the PLC switches to STOP due to a processor error, a rack connection error or an inter-rack cable connection error. The options available are as follows:
  • Fallback	- Select if outputs should fallback to their configured fallback values.
  • Maintain	- Select if outputs should maintain their previous healthy values.

This DFB is to be used in conjunction with the X80_DDO1602Out block. The X80_DDO1602Out block is used to write parameters to the module.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="5">The module status is healthy (oOK) provided:
- The CRA network module (iLnkOK) is healthy; AND
- The module is reporting healthy.
Note: The MOD_HEALTH is a global health status and includes all fault statuses in MOD_FLT.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="93"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="2">Map out the channel error bits for HMI display.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="166"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="2">Map out the fault status byte for diagnostics
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="76"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="10">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	18/03/2020	Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="60"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
