					<textBox width="70" height="10">Revision History
==========================================================================================================================================
1.00	BCY	18/03/2020	Initial Release
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="60"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="13">==========================================================================================================================================
FUNCTION BLOCK -	X80_DDO1602Out
==========================================================================================================================================
Description:		X80 BMX DDO1602 16 Channel Digital Output Module Output
Date Changed:		18/03/2020
Change Comments:	Initial Release
Revision:		1.00

==========================================================================================================================================
Copyright Rio TInto Pty Ltd, 2020
==========================================================================================================================================
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="0"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="45">Description:
==========================================================================================================================================
This DFB is used to write parameters to a X80 BMX DDO1602 16 Channel Digital Output module.

The DFB satisfies the following requirements:
• The channel data (iCh00-iCh15) are mapped to the T_U_DIS_STD_OUT_16 Device DDT.

The BMX DDO1602 module must have the following parameters set:
SUPPLY MONITORING - Sets the power supply monitoring function for the 16 channels on or off. It is enabled by default.

REACTIVATE - Defines the reactivation mode of outputs tripped by overloads or short-circuits. The options available are as follows:
  • Programmed	- Do not use.
  • Automatic	- Select.

FALLBACK MODE - Defines the fallback mode adopted by outputs when the PLC switches to STOP due to a processor error, a rack connection error or an inter-rack cable connection error. The options available are as follows:
  • Fallback	- Select if outputs should fallback to their configured fallback values.
  • Maintain	- Select if outputs should maintain their previous healthy values.

This DFB is to be used in conjunction with the X80_DDO1602In block. The X80_DDO1602In block is used to unmap the input data from the module.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="14"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
					<textBox width="70" height="5">Map the digital output channel data to the T_U_DIS_STD_OUT_16 Device DDT.  The BIT_TO_WORD / WORD_TO_BIT logic is a useful way of doing 16 move instructions.

The output channels are not masked by the module health as this should to be managed by the logic external to the DFB. This allows outputs to continue being controlled in the event not all channels fail.
    <objPosition posX="0" posY="73"></objPosition>
					</textBox>
				</networkFBD>
			</FBDSource>
		</FBProgram>
	</FBSource>
</VariablesExchangeFile>
